From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:46:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Reconnect an EventSource whose stream ends with a
 network error

An EventSource reestablished its connection when the body of the event
stream ended without a network error, and did nothing when it ended with
one, so it stayed open and never reconnected. That happens today when the
stream fails to decode; net reports a stream cut short by the connection
as complete, so a dropped connection was reestablished, but it will
report it as a network error.

The specification only reestablishes the connection when the body ends
without a network error, as the end-of-body steps do not run for a body
that errors. Firefox and Chrome reestablish a connection that drops while
the stream is read. Do the same: when the body of an announced connection
ends with a network error, reestablish the connection, or fail it if the
error is one that makes that futile, as for a network error in place of
the response. A network error in place of the response is still handled
only once, when the response arrives.

Validation: New test `tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/eventsource-network-error.window.js` passes with this patch, before and after `net: End a body cut short by the connection with a network error`; with that patch but without this one, it times out.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote this patch and its test following docs/fetch-p4a-truncated-body-audit-2026-10-22.md in the workspace, and applied an independent review's findings)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
